// setup.eeai - your own script for every game started on this PC. Age of AI reads it at each game's start and calls
// its hooks from 2 s game time on:
//
//   on_game()       every new game, before the game type's own hook
//   on_skirmish()   a random-map game
//   on_scenario()   a scenario (the scenario editor's test play too)
//   on_campaign()   a campaign's scenario
//
// A hook is a script: let, if, for, wait(10s), triggers and timers, the players (player(2).gold += 500) and the
// control pipe's commands as functions (spawn(2, unit.inf02_spearman, 70, 50, 10)). What is written outside the
// hooks runs first, in every game: a let there is a name all hooks share. A hook that isn't needed may be deleted.
//
// A saved game carries on what the hooks started (variables, timers, triggers), a hook that still waits (wait(...))
// where it stands. Not run: a multiplayer game, the scenario editor itself.
// A mistake is told in the game and in ageofai_log.csv, with its line; ageofai_check.exe checks the file without the
// game.

on_game() {
}

on_skirmish() {
}

on_scenario() {
}

on_campaign() {
}
